~ start
RITCHIE: Ba-bye, Ollie! I swear I'll make your gift the biggest surprise ever! Just so you wait!

I'm glad that we're friends but I hope it is not a used eraser like last year.

OLLIE: Okay! It better be good! Ba-bye, Ritchie! 

#SFX: Puk! 

A hand hits the back of my head. It doesn't hurt but it makes me jump.

It was Kuya Dodong and his proud smile after what seemed like executing a flawless combo in his gameboy. He didn't even look up from the screen and tried to act cool like he wasn't waiting for me. 

DODONG: Over here, slowpoke! Did Ma'am Santos make you clean the whole board with your face? We've been standing here for ages! 

Behind him, my younger brother, Noni, was trying to do something. In desperation, he tries to tilt the empty plastic cup in a downward angle to lick the leftover sauce and catch the very last piece of food. 

NONI: Kuya Ollie! Kuya Dodong bought fishballs earlier but he didn't give me the crunchy bits at the bottom! He ate all of it! Grrrr. He is so greedy! 

DODONG: Because you dropped yours on the dirt, Noni. Anyway, Ollie, let's go.

#SFX: Ting-ting-ting! 

I looked across the street as the street vendors were lined up under the big narra tree.
It was the sound of the dirty ice cream bell ringing, but the aroma in the air smelled like sweet banana cue. People were also crowding to buy toys.

OLLIE: Kuya, can I go look at the vendors over there? I will be super fast! Promise!

DODONG: ...
DODONG: Since I am the best Kuya in the universe, okay. Here is exactly twenty pesos. 
DODONG: Lucky for you, I saved some change from my lunch allowance today. 
DODONG: Don't lose it and don't take forever! Tatay will be here soon.

OLLIE: Thank you, Kuya! 

=> END